WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.691
In this video, you will add a local business as a sponsor of your contest, with its logo and website, so it gets thanked on your contest page.

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:09.851
We start on the map.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.812
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:16.937
That is the only address you need.

00:00:19.015 --> 00:00:21.421
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:25.165
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:26.503
Tap Use my location.

00:00:28.444 --> 00:00:32.881
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:32.881 --> 00:00:36.086
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:40.646
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:44.681 --> 00:00:47.370
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.566
See the three dots?

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:52.868
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:53.406
Tap them.

00:00:55.042 --> 00:00:56.680
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.018
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:01:03.741 --> 00:01:04.323
Tap Mine.

00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:05.955
This is your personal page.

00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:11.314
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:15.049
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:18.721
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:24.170
A sponsor is a local business that supports your contest.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.042
Their name and logo show on your contest page.

00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:27.836
Tap Sponsors.

00:01:29.647 --> 00:01:32.286
Type the sponsor's name, and choose a tier.

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:35.705
Sponsors are listed by tier, so the top tier shows first.

00:01:37.814 --> 00:01:41.145
Add their website, so people can click through.

00:01:41.145 --> 00:01:42.811
Then choose their logo.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:48.224
Use a clear picture, a J P G, P N G, or WebP file under six hundred kilobytes.

00:01:50.108 --> 00:01:51.227
Tap Add sponsor.

00:01:51.227 --> 00:01:56.028
Sponsors can support your contest directly, and any payment goes to you.

00:01:56.028 --> 00:01:59.580
One rule is important: payment never affects who wins.

00:02:01.517 --> 00:02:08.557
To check how it looks, tap See it as voters do, and you will see the sponsors on the contest page, just as your neighbors do.

00:02:10.544 --> 00:02:13.446
Next up: Presenting installer and quote requests.
